# The vault is Markdown read by Obsidian on whatever platform, and the digests
# are dated snapshots that must not show as modified just because a generator
# ran on Windows. LF in the repo and in the working tree, everywhere.
#
# The writers pass newline="\n" explicitly as well. Both belong: this settles
# what git stores and checks out, the argument settles what a script writes
# before git ever sees it.
*.md text eol=lf

# The crosswalk registry and its attestation record, for the same reason. The
# attestation file is rewritten wholesale by `crosswalk.py --attest`, so without
# this it shows as modified after every run that changed nothing.
*.yaml text eol=lf
